      "statement": "For every N>=2 and secret s, n=ceil(log2N), the SINGLE QUDIT-LOG2-R63 algorithm reproduced in proof.md and qudit_decoder.md recovers the full secret with unconditional probability>=1-2^-8 on independent ideal coset copies. Main n>=2^48 uses exact finite rational RLOG, m=ceil(RLOG(n)^2), actual-width tapered trees, explicit Clifford+T frequency-bin/Fourier vector data measurements, per-root Ct, ONE global fine-attempt capA=4Lblk, fixed selected Qcap=Ct*(Kc*(Y+6+E)+A)+Kp and raw Qbank=1024Qcap including ALL discards/padding. All physical odd/twoadic and finite exhaustive branches are reproduced. Every source,failed/missing/retried root,abort,lookup,address,bit operation,compiler/circuit generation,initialization,gate,measurement and reset is charged; all four bounds hold JOINTLY on EVERY branch. F(n)=n sum_(j=1)^63 (-1)^(j-1)(log2n)^(-2j)+(1/2)(log2n)^2 is the complete exact64-term exponent; proof15 proves it upperbounds the actual rounded geometry and improves time/SC by an unbounded ratio. Resource logarithms usepositive n2 envelopes atn1. Total charged work O(n^3 (log2n) 2^F(n)), exact growthindex1.",
